drm: h713-afbd: do not offer the firmware's zoom aspect

0133 exposed the six display aspect modes of the firmware's window manager
as the plane's "aspect" enum. Two of them were measured then (auto and
proportional, doku/nachtlog/S15); "zoom" (kHalDisplayAspectRatio_Zoom, 5)
never was. It is not usable.

On the HY310, kernel 6.18.38, a 1920x1080p60 source from a ThinkPad and
the warp off, h713-tv ctl aspect zoom takes the plane down and up as every
aspect change does. The firmware does not take the plane again: the video
enable and the video disable handshake both end in "READY did not clear
(00000001)", h713-tv sees the capture's flip pointers stand still ("no
signal") and the picture does not come back, while the source keeps
sending 1920x1080@60 (its xrandr). With "aspect = zoom" saved, the next
cold start did the same 0.1 s after the signal locked, with no click at
all. Measured 06.10.2026, journal and dmesg of both boots.

So the enum no longer lists it. The DRM core refuses a value that is not
in the list, h713-tv answers "aspect does not know" and drops a saved
"zoom" at its start with a line in the journal. The enum value stays, as
the firmware's numbering.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -314,6 +314,12 @@
  * why it is the default here; "auto" stays selectable for the record.
  * Shell and RPC paths for this setting are stubs in the firmware; the
  * descriptor word is the only one that lives.
+ *
+ * "zoom" (5) is the firmware's too, but it is not offered: with it in word
+ * 35 the firmware does not take the plane any more. On the HY310 with a
+ * 1920x1080p60 source the enable and the disable handshake both time out
+ * ("READY did not clear") and the capture stops for good; a saved "zoom"
+ * did the same at the next start, with no click at all (06.10.2026).
  */
 enum h713_aspect {
 	H713_ASPECT_AUTO = 0,
@@ -332,7 +338,6 @@
 	{ H713_ASPECT_FULL, "full" },
 	{ H713_ASPECT_16_9, "16:9" },
 	{ H713_ASPECT_4_3, "4:3" },
-	{ H713_ASPECT_ZOOM, "zoom" },
 };
 
